H3800.definition:
from H3799 (כָּתַם);
properly, something carved out, i.e. ore; hence, gold (pure as originally mined)
KJV: ((most) fine, pure) gold(-en wedge).

H3801.definition:
or כֻּתֹּנֶת; from an unused root meaning to cover (compare H3802 (כָּתֵף));
a shirt
KJV: coat, garment, robe.

H3802.definition:
from an unused root meaning to clothe;
the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything
KJV: arm, corner, shoulder(-piece), side, undersetter.

H3803.definition:
a primitive root;
to enclose; hence (in a friendly sense) to crown, (in a hostile one) to besiege; also to wait (as restraining oneself)
KJV: beset round, compass about, be crowned inclose round, suffer.

H3804.definition:
from H3803 (כָּתַר);
properly, a circlet, i.e. a diadem
KJV: crown.

H3805.definition:
feminine active participle of H3803 (כָּתַר);
the capital of a column
KJV: chapiter.

H3806.definition:
a primitive root;
to butt or pound
KJV: bray.

H3807.definition:
a primitive root;
to bruise or violently strike
KJV: beat (down, to pieces), break in pieces, crushed, destroy, discomfit, smite, stamp. l

H3808.definition:
or לוֹא; or לֹה; (Deuteronomy 3:11), a primitive particle;
not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no; often used with other particles
KJV: [idiom] before, [phrase] or else, ere, [phrase] except, ig(-norant), much, less, nay, neither, never, no((-ne), -r, (-thing)), ([idiom] as though...,(can-), for) not (out of), of nought, otherwise, out of, [phrase] surely, [phrase] as truly as, [phrase] of a truth, [phrase] verily, for want, [phrase] whether, without.

H3809.definition:
(Aramaic) or לָה; (Aramaic) (Daniel 4:32), corresponding to H3808 (לֹא)
{not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no;}
KJV: or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.

H3810.definition:
or לוֹ דבַר; (Samuel 9:4,5), or לִדְבִר; (Joshua 13:26), (probably rather לֹדְבַר ); from H3808 (לֹא) and H1699 (דֹּבֶר); pastureless;
Lo-Debar, a place in Palestine
KJV: Debir, Lodebar.

H3811.definition:
a primitive root;
to tire; (figuratively) to be (or make) disgusted
KJV: faint, grieve, lothe, (be, make) weary (selves).

H3812.definition:
from H3811 (לָאָה); weary;
Leah, a wife of Jacob
KJV: Leah.

H3813.definition:
a primitive root;
to muffle
KJV: cover.

H3814.definition:
from H3813 (לָאַט) (or perhaps for active participle of H3874 (לוּט));
properly, muffled, i.e. silently
KJV: softly.

H3815.definition:
from the prepositional prefix and H410 (אֵל); (belonging) to God;
Lael an Israelite
KJV: Lael.

H3816.definition:
or לְאוֹם; from an unused root meaning to gather;
a community
KJV: nation, people.

H3817.definition:
plural of H3816 (לְאֹם); communities;
Leum mim, an Arabian
KJV: Leummim.

H3818.definition:
from H3808 (לֹא) and H5971 (עַם) with pronominal suffix; not my people;
Lo-Ammi, the symbolic name of a son of Hosea
KJV: Lo-ammi.

H3819.definition:
from H3808 (לֹא) and H7355 (רָחַם); not pitied;
Lo-Ruchamah, the symbolic name of a son of Hosea
KJV: Lo-ruhamah.

H3820.definition:
a form of H3824 (לֵבָב);
the heart; also used (figuratively) very widely for the feelings, the will and even the intellect; likewise for the centre of anything
KJV: [phrase] care for, comfortably, consent, [idiom] considered, courag(-eous), friend(-ly), ((broken-), (hard-), (merry-), (stiff-), (stout-), double) heart(-ed), [idiom] heed, [idiom] I, kindly, midst, mind(-ed), [idiom] regard(-ed), [idiom] themselves, [idiom] unawares, understanding, [idiom] well, willingly, wisdom.

H3821.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3820 (לֵב)
{the heart; also used (figuratively) very widely for the feelings, the will and even the intellect; likewise for the centre of anything}
KJV: heart.

H3822.definition:
plural of H3833 (לָבִיא); lionesses;
Lebaoth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lebaoth. See also H1034 (בֵּית לְבָאוֹת).

H3824.definition:
from H3823 (לָבַב); used also like H3820 (לֵב)
the heart (as the most interior organ);
KJV: [phrase] bethink themselves, breast, comfortably, courage, ((faint), (tender-) heart(-ed), midst, mind, [idiom] unawares, understanding.

H3825.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3824 (לֵבָב)
{the heart (as the most interior organ);}
KJV: heart.

H3826.definition:
feminine of H3820 (לֵב);
the heart
KJV: heart.

H3828.definition:
or לְבֹנָה; from H3836 (לָבָן);
frankincense (from its whiteness or perhaps that of its smoke)
KJV: (frank-) incense.

H3829.definition:
the same as H3828 (לְבוֹנָה);
Lebonah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lebonah.

H3830.definition:
or לְבֻשׁ; from H3847 (לָבַשׁ);
a garment (literally or figuratively); by implication (euphemistically) a wife
KJV: apparel, clothed with, clothing, garment, raiment, vestment, vesture.

H3831.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3830 (לְבוּשׁ)
{a garment (literally or figuratively); by implication (euphemistically) a wife}
KJV: garment.

H3832.definition:
a primitive root;
to overthrow; intransposed, to fall
KJV: fall.

H3834.definition:
or rather לְבִבָה; from H3823 (לָבַב) in its original sense of fatness (or perhaps of folding);
a cake (either as fried or turned)
KJV: cake.

H3836.definition:
or (Genesis 49:12) לָבֵן; from H3835 (לָבַן);
white
KJV: white.

H3837.definition:
the same as H3836 (לָבָן);
Laban, a Mesopotamian; also a place in the Desert
KJV: Laban.

H3838.definition:
or לְבָנָה; the same as H3842 (לְבָנָה);
Lebana or Lebanah, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Lebana, Lebanah.

H3839.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן);
some sort of whitish tree, perhaps the storax
KJV: poplar.

H3840.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן);
properly, whiteness, i.e. (by implication) transparency
KJV: paved.

H3841.definition:
the same as H3839 (לִבְנֶה);
Libnah, a place in the Desert and one in Palestine
KJV: Libnah.

H3842.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן);
properly, (the) white, i.e. the moon
KJV: moon. See also H3838 (לְבָנָא).

H3843.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן);
a brick (from the whiteness of the clay)
KJV: (altar of) brick, tile.

H3844.definition:
from H3825 (לְבַב); (the) white mountain (from its snow);
Lebanon, a mountain range in Palestine
KJV: Lebanon.

H3845.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן); white;
Libni, an Israelite
KJV: Libni.

H3846.definition:
patronymically from H3845 (לִבְנִי);
a Libnite or descendants of Libni (collectively)
KJV: Libnites.

H3847.definition:
or לָבֵשׁ; a primitive root;
properly, wrap around, i.e. (by implication) to put on agarment or clothe (oneself, or another), literally or figuratively
KJV: (in) apparel, arm, array (self), clothe (self), come upon, put (on, upon), wear.

H3848.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3847 (לָבַשׁ)
{properly, wrap around, i.e. (by implication) to put on agarment or clothe (oneself, or another), literally or figuratively}
KJV: clothe.

H3849.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to deepen or hollow (like H3537 (כַּד));
a log or measure forliquids
KJV: log (of oil).

H3850.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain signification;
Lod, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lod.

H3851.definition:
from an usused root meaning to gleam;
a flash; figuratively, a sharply polished blade or point of aweapon
KJV: blade, bright, flame, glittering.

H3852.definition:
or לַהֶבֶת; feminine of H3851 (לַהַב), and meaning the same
{a flash; figuratively, a sharply polished blade or point of aweapon}
KJV: flame(-ming), head (of a spear).

H3853.definition:
plural of H3851 (לַהַב); flames;
Lehabim, a son of Mizraim, and his descendants
KJV: Lehabim.

H3854.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be eager;
intense mental application
KJV: study.

H3855.definition:
from an unused root meaning to glow (compare H3851 (לַהַב)) or else to be earnest (compare H3854 (לַהַג));
Lahad, an Israelite
KJV: Lahad.

H3857.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to lick, i.e. (by implication) to blaze
KJV: burn (up), set on fire, flaming, kindle.

H3858.definition:
from H3857 (לָהַט);
a blaze; also (from the idea of enwrapping) magic (as covert)
KJV: flaming, enchantment.

H3859.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to burn in, i.e. (figuratively) to rankle
KJV: wound.

H3860.definition:
from the prepositional prefix meaning to or for and H2005 (הֵן);
popularly for if; hence, therefore
KJV: for them (by mistake for prepositional suffix).

H3861.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3860 (לָהֵן);
therefore; also except
KJV: but, except, save, therefore, wherefore.

H3862.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to gather;
an assembly
KJV: company.

H3863.definition:
or לֻא; or לוּ;
a conditional particle; if; by implication (interj. as a wish) would that!
KJV: if (haply), peradventure, I pray thee, though, I would, would God (that).

H3865.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
Lud, the name of two nations
KJV: Lud, Lydia.

H3866.definition:
or לוּדִיִּי; patrial from H3865 (לוּד);
a Ludite or inhabitants of Lud (only in plural)
KJV: Ludim. Lydians.

H3867.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to twine, i.e. (by implication) to unite, to remain; also to borrow (as a form of obligation) or (caus.) to lend
KJV: abide with, borrow(-er), cleave, join (self), lend(-er).

H3869.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
some kind of nuttree, perhaps the almond
KJV: hazel.

H3870.definition:
probably from H3869 (לוּז) (as growing there);
Luz, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Luz.

H3871.definition:
or לֻחַ; from a primitive root;
probably meaning to glisten; a tablet (as polished), of stone, wood or metal
KJV: board, plate, table.

H3872.definition:
or לֻחוֹת; (Jeremiah 48:5), from the same as H3871 (לוּחַ); floored;
Luchith, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Luhith.

H3873.definition:
active participle of H3907 (לָחַשׁ); (the) enchanter;
Lochesh, an Israelite
KJV: Hallohesh, Haloshesh (includ. the article).

H3874.definition:
a primitive root;
to wrap up
KJV: cast, wrap.

H3875.definition:
from H3874 (לוּט);
a veil
KJV: covering.

H3876.definition:
the same as H3875 (לוֹט);
Lot, Abraham's nephew
KJV: Lot.

H3877.definition:
from H3875 (לוֹט); covering;
Lotan, an Idumaean
KJV: Lotan.

H3878.definition:
from H3867 (לָוָה); attached;
Levi, a son of Jacob
KJV: Levi. See also H3879 (לֵוִי), H3881 (לֵוִיִּי).

H3879.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3880 (לִוְיָה)
{something attached, i.e. a wreath}
KJV: Levite.

H3880.definition:
from H3867 (לָוָה);
something attached, i.e. a wreath
KJV: ornament.

H3881.definition:
or לֵוִי; patronymically from H3878 (לֵוִי);
a Levite or descendant of Levi
KJV: Leviite.

H3882.definition:
from H3867 (לָוָה);
a wreathed animal, i.e. a serpent (especially the crocodile or some other large sea-monster); figuratively, the constellation of the dragon; also as a symbol of Babylon
KJV: leviathan, mourning.

H3883.definition:
from an unused root meaning to fold back;
a spiral step
KJV: winding stair. Compare H3924 (לֻלָאָה).

H3884.definition:
or לוּלֵי; from H3863 (לוּא) and H3808 (לֹא);
if not
KJV: except, had not, if (...not), unless, were it not that.

H3885.definition:
or לִין; a primitive root;
to stop (usually over night); by implication, to stay permanently; hence (in a bad sense) to be obstinate (especially in words, to complain)
KJV: abide (all night), continue, dwell, endure, grudge, be left, lie all night, (cause to) lodge (all night, in, -ing, this night), (make to) murmur, remain, tarry (all night, that night).

H3886.definition:
a primitive root;
to gulp; figuratively, to be rash
KJV: swallow down (up).

H3887.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to make mouths at, i.e. to scoff; hence (from the effort to pronounce a foreign language) to interpret, or (generally) intercede
KJV: ambassador, have in derision, interpreter, make a mock, mocker, scorn(-er, -ful), teacher.

H3888.definition:
a primitive root;
to knead
KJV: knead.

H3889.definition:
from H3888 (לוּשׁ); kneading;
Lush, a place in Palestine
KJV: Laish (from the margin). Compare H3919 (לַיִשׁ).

H3890.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3867 (לָוָה);
properly, adhesion, i.e. (as preposition) with
KJV: [idiom] thee.

H3892.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be new;
fresh, i.e. unused or undried
KJV: green, moist.

H3893.definition:
from the same as H3892 (לַח);
freshness, i.e. vigor
KJV: natural force.

H3894.definition:
or לָחֻם; passive participle of H3898 (לָחַם);
properly, eaten, i.e. food; also flesh, i.e. body
KJV: while...is eating, flesh.

H3895.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be soft;
the cheek (from its fleshiness); hence, the jaw-bone
KJV: cheek (bone), jaw (bone).

H3896.definition:
a form of H3895 (לְחִי);
Lechi, a place in Palestine
KJV: Lehi. Compare also H7437 (רָמַת לֶחִי).

H3897.definition:
a primitive root;
to lick
KJV: lick (up).

H3898.definition:
a primitive root;
to feed on; figuratively, to consume; by implication, to battle (as destruction)
KJV: devour, eat, [idiom] ever, fight(-ing), overcome, prevail, (make) war(-ring).

H3899.definition:
from H3898 (לָחַם); See also H1036 (בֵּית לְעַפְרָה)
food (for man or beast), especially bread, or grain (for making it)
KJV: (shew-) bread, [idiom] eat, food, fruit, loaf, meat, victuals.
